    <expertiseList>
      <Value>
{"layout":{"Umbraco.BlockList":[{"contentUdi":"umb://element/78c8242998da425fa8eba69b0df4d9cb"},{"contentUdi":"umb://element/6fa4dde013c5465abc2a5e6abc92f590"},{"contentUdi":"umb://element/09ecbf1cd6774e5b82d9f089cdf50c17"}]},"contentData":[{"contentTypeKey":"338ac17e-85de-40c4-8028-34adf753b3c6","udi":"umb://element/78c8242998da425fa8eba69b0df4d9cb","PropType":null,"stringItemText":"Soil Testing"},{"contentTypeKey":"338ac17e-85de-40c4-8028-34adf753b3c6","udi":"umb://element/6fa4dde013c5465abc2a5e6abc92f590","PropType":null,"stringItemText":"Concrete Strength Testing"},{"contentTypeKey":"338ac17e-85de-40c4-8028-34adf753b3c6","udi":"umb://element/09ecbf1cd6774e5b82d9f089cdf50c17","PropType":null,"stringItemText":"Asphalt Verification and Testing"}],"settingsData":[]}
</Value>
    </expertiseList>
    <grid>
      <Value>
{"layout":{"Umbraco.BlockGrid":[{"contentUdi":"umb://element/2e5d22d7ad784656b849a4605ada73c0","areas":[],"columnSpan":12,"rowSpan":1}]},"contentData":[{"contentTypeKey":"9a4f7c2e-1b3d-4e8a-bf01-7d62a8f5c930","udi":"umb://element/2e5d22d7ad784656b849a4605ada73c0","content":"\u003cdiv class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"758bl\" data-offset-key=\"dadl7-0-0\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"dadl7-0-0\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"dadl7-0-0\"\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAs Roadlab’s footprint grows, so does the responsibility behind every result we issue.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMaintaining trust across multiple laboratories, regions, and disciplines requires more than compliance — it demands continuous learning, strong systems, and people who understand the consequences of getting it wrong. Today we are sharing a closer look at how that responsibility is carried in practice.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"/media/u40dna5g/polokwane.jpg\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class=\"heading-h3\"\u003eExpanding our Accredited Network\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFollowing extensive preparation throughout 2025, the Polokwane branch has completed its accreditation audit and is now awaiting formal confirmation for its ISO 17205 accreditation.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOnce approved, this will become Roadlab’s first accredited facility in Limpopo — a significant step in improving access to accreditation-assured testing for mining operations, border infrastructure, and major civil works across the country’s northern regions. \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUntil now, Roadlab’s most northerly accredited facility was located in Gauteng. The Polokwane\u003cbr\u003eaccreditation changes that reality. It brings verified testing capability closer to many of our sites and\u003cbr\u003eaffirms that the same rigorous standards define Roadlab’s accredited network nationwide.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"/media/3apn355g/tanzania.jpg\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class=\"heading-h3\"\u003ePreparing for the Next Standard\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAccreditation at Roadlab is not treated as a compliance exercise, but as an ongoing discipline. Group Quality Manager Janco Potgieter is currently in Tanzania supporting preparations for a PJLA accreditation audit, reinforcing Roadlab’s approach to quality beyond South Africa’s borders. \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOur Bloemfontein laboratory will undergo reaccreditation in February, followed by Bellville in April. These reviews are approached proactively — using internal audits, method reviews, and corrective actions to strengthen systems well ahead of formal assessment.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eReaccreditation provides an opportunity to reassess processes, verify consistency across teams, and ensure that documented systems reflect how work is actually done in the laboratory and on site. It is a deliberate decision to hold established branches to the same scrutiny as new facilities — and to improve them as expectations evolve.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"/media/mp4fzxv1/uj.jpg\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class=\"heading-h3\"\u003eBuilding Capability Through Colloboration\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn February, the women of Roadlab’s Quality team will attend the Women in Laboratories Africa Conference at the University of Johannesburg at the end of the month — a focused, working conference built around how laboratories across Africa are managed, improved, and future-proofed.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is event is about exposure to how other accredited laboratories approach risk, technology adoption, skills development, and day-to-day quality decision-making — from technical execution to administrative control. \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe programme is centred on practical knowledge exchange: round-table discussions, skills training, peer problem-solving, and direct engagement with laboratory professionals responsible for maintaining standards under real operational pressure.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor Roadlab, this matters because trust is maintained by staying current, curious, and connected. Our quality systems are not static — they evolve through learning, shared experience, and informed judgement. \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEngaging with peers, new technologies, and emerging best practices strengthens our ability to safeguard results, support our teams, and maintain credibility across every laboratory we operate.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class=\"heading-h3\"\u003eYou will find us at the forefront of quality assurance. Why?\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEvery presentation, every audit, and every new laboratory we establish has a single purpose — to strengthen confidence in  results.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBy embedding testing at the source, refining analytical methods, and continuously improving how our systems perform, Roadlab is advancing the standards that define quality assurance in our world.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eBecause our standards are the future of testing.\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"/media/1wkn2s1i/dangote-quality-assurance-work.jpg\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}],"settingsData":[]}
</Value>
    </grid>
    <heroContent>
      <Value><![CDATA[{
  "markup": "<p>From supporting international accreditation efforts to expanding access to accredited testing, the past month reflects how quality is sustained in practice. Constant preparation, travel, review, and engagement across our network ensures every result we issue can be relied on, wherever it is produced.</p>",
  "blocks": {
    "contentData": [],
    "settingsData": []
  }
}]]></Value>
